  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that 6-Methoxysorigenin may interact with UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4 through multiple indirect pathways. The first pathway links 6-Methoxysorigenin to the inner centromere protein, which in turn targets UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4. The second pathway connects 6-Methoxysorigenin to multidrug resistance-associated protein 7, which targets isobutyl hexanoate, which also targets UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4. The third pathway similarly links 6-Methoxysorigenin to multidrug resistance-associated protein 7, which targets another compound that ultimately targets UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4. These findings indicate that 6-Methoxysorigenin may exert its effects on UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4 through a series of intermediate targets, suggesting a complex regulatory network. The evidence is consistent across different pathways, but the strength of the association varies, with the first and third pathways having slightly higher scores. The mechanisms involve targeting of proteins that ultimately influence the activity of UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B4, highlighting a potential role in drug metabolism or disease regulation.",
